(text "TPS3700: 9.2 V UV rising / 19.2 V OV rising nominal. Open-drain outputs wired together.\n74LVC08: ENi = CMDi AND WINDOW_OK; each command has a 10k pulldown.\nEach outlet also has an EN pulldown: reset, missing logic supply and disconnected command request OFF.\nA voltage recovery can re-enable an asserted command and reset a latched breaker; firmware must deassert on unexpected PG loss.\nShared inhibit is a common failure point, not a redundant safety channel. Local eFuse OVLO remains independent.\nThis circuit does not disconnect VIN from the regulator, heater stages or eFuse input pins." (at 25.4000 226.0600 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d74f0ff1-41a8-5e64-a431-f074b2e20799"))
